f 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282381 1111 #uuid "0e443c42-f7c3-5a7d-9372-336d4a18c4b3" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282382 1034 "x\\ge -1" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282382 1111 #uuid "db47709a-b0ea-5668-9018-7e6bbb5e1510" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282383 1034 "x>0" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282383 1111 #uuid "bbf07bbc-2a17-5959-a4cd-7e83c405f04e" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282385 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1089 "q-88040" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-4<\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1).$" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1113 #uuid "c0f1922a-ec31-5441-90dc-f80b17594035" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282384 1145 "We use each side of the inequality as an exponent of $e.$ This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-4} & <{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}\\cdot {e}^{-4} & <{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)} \\\\ (x+1){e}^{-4} & <x-1 \\\\ (x+1) & <(x-1){e}^{4} \\\\ x+1 & <x{e}^{4}-{e}^{4} \\\\ 1+{e}^{4} & <x({e}^{4}-1) \\\\ \\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1} & <x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithms in the original inequality. To find the domain of the logarithms, we recall that the argument of the logarithm must be positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & >-1 \\\\ x-1 & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x>\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1},\\infty ).$ Additionally, the domains of the logarithms are $x>-1$ and $x>1,$ which can be expressed as $(-1,\\infty )$ and $(1,\\infty )$ respectively. To find the solutions that are in the domains of the logarithms, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1},\\infty )\\cap (-1,\\infty )\\cap (1,\\infty )=(\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1},\\infty )\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in (\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1},\\infty ),$ which can also be written as $x>\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}.$" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282386 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282387 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282388 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282389 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282390 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1041 "selection" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282387 13194139534207 true] [17592186282385 1110 #uuid "8a445833-b804-548d-80d1-18b5934452d7" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282386 1034 "-1<x<\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282386 1111 #uuid "319337f9-7abd-5450-82fd-5ba98710ba30" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282387 1034 "x>\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282387 1111 #uuid "b1ef25e4-af35-5b94-bde3-e24f8a8bb41e" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282388 1034 "0<x<\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282388 1111 #uuid "39499c94-8f4a-5365-ab5b-75b64ed3be7b" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282389 1034 "x<\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [17592186282389 1111 #uuid "52d9c87d-2970-518b-9a45-960ee4c4f17d" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282390 1034 "1<x<\\frac{1+{e}^{4}}{{e}^{4}-1}" 13194139534207 true] [17592186282390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534207 true] [175921862